    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "PRINTING VALUES\n\nEvery print node takes one kind of value. The compiler also converts for you where it is safe:\n  - any value wired into a String pin becomes text (5 -> \"5\", true -> \"true\")\n  - an integer wired into a decimal (f64) pin is widened automatically.\nSo you can wire a number straight into Print String without a conversion node.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          210.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "PRINT NODES\nprint_number takes a decimal, print_bool a boolean. print_formatted takes a template and three values. log_warn / log_error mark the line with a severity.",
        "position": [
          360.0,
          -70.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1260.0,
          110.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
